WEBVTT

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:14.070
I-Is that...

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.930
...a spaceship?

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:18.540
That can't be...

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:28.210
Shun! Yuuta!

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.470
It finally begins.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.560
An alien?

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:51.030
Congratulations, representatives of Earth.

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:58.360
You have won the preliminaries for Grand Celesta Galaxy and earned the right to proceed into the main tournament.

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:00.740
Say that again?

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:02.780
What's going on here?

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:05.270
What? What is he saying?

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:08.500
Did he just say...?

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.500
That we are representatives of Earth?

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:14.150
That's right.

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:17.460
You are not representatives of the country known as Japan.

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:21.470
Not Japan... but Earth?

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:28.560
As I suspected, I see you have been fighting without being told any knowledge of the details.

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:30.520
What did you do to Shun and Yuuta?!

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:33.810
What did you do to the spectators?

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:37.020
I've put them to sleep.

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:39.480
Sleep?

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:41.640
Why would you do that?

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:43.870
I'll explain from here.

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:49.960
Gouenji-san!

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:53.370
I'm sorry, Tenma.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:56.670
I had you guys fight without revealing to you the real situation.

00:03:57.220 --> 00:03:58.380
What do you mean?

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:03.430
I'll tell you everything about what's happening right now.

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:08.970
Do you know about the incident 3 months ago, when the moon could no longer be seen in the sky?

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:10.280
Yes...

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:12.940
The news said that we could no longer observe the moon from Earth.

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:20.940
As I recall, it was because a large amount of cosmic dust broke out, blocking light so that we can't see it anymore...

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:23.520
No, that's wrong.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:27.490
Yes, completely wrong.

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:31.950
This is absurd.

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:35.620
Do you take me for a fool?

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:37.000
It's true.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.500
It is a reality that has been thrusted upon you humankind.

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:49.970
We want you to participate in the soccer tournament Grand Celesta Galaxy, which is taking place 188,000 light years away in the Milky Way.

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:53.930
I do not have time to be listening to your jokes.

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:57.770
If you refuse to participate, this planet is doomed.

00:04:58.570 --> 00:04:59.860
That's enough.

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:08.080
I see you don't understand the situation you are in.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:09.070
Very well then.

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:11.740
I'll just have to show you.

00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:21.250
What did you bring me here for?

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:28.470
What?

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:07.630
I have used our special weapon to erase that natural satellite for your planet, which you call the moon.

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:10.890
I don't believe this.

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:21.060
Now the tilt of your Earth's axis will begin to shift.

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:26.990
If you don't do anything, Earth will undergo a slew of natural disasters before it eventually destroys itself.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:33.530
Your only way to save yourselves is to rely on our help.

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:41.440
Now do you understand?

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:46.430
You cannot turn down our proposal.

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:54.010
We don't even have room for negotiations?

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:55.660
Yes.

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:59.020
It's the same as if someone placed the edge of a sword at Earth's throat.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:04.520
So the fate of Earth rests on that tournament.

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:08.360
This matter involves soccer...

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:10.780
Would you allow me to handle it?

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:14.540
I promise to leave results that will lead to hope.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:16.700
Very well.

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:18.910
I'm counting on you, Gouenji-kun.

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:21.440
Earth's very existence is on the line.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:23.040
I will do everything in my power to help you.

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:35.120
Listen closely, citizens of this remote planet.

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:42.400
I am Bitway Ozrock, sent to you by the Council of the Galaxy Union. {銀河連邦評議会}

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:47.080
If I were to use your words...

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:50.440
I suppose I would be called an alien.

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:57.410
Everyone, silence please! Listen to what he has to say!

00:07:58.220 --> 00:08:05.270
188,000 light years from this planet, there is a sun called Falamdite.

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:14.640
Within that solar system, there exists a planet called Falam Orbius that is inhabited by intelligent life, similar to your planet.

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:24.770
However, due to the sudden appearance of a black hole, Falam Orbius is destined to die within months.

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:38.970
They have been condemned to death.

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:47.580
Therefore, they have declared a war of aggression upon other planets across the galaxy, so that they may survive.

00:08:49.330 --> 00:08:53.480
However, war that encompasses the galaxy wouldn't be what you call a smart method.

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:57.590
We have proposed a different solution to Falam Orbius.

00:08:58.460 --> 00:09:03.730
The appearance of the black hole is a calamity that has occurred in the galaxy itself.

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:08.310
Naturally, all species that live in said galaxy will wish to survive.

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:19.200
Therefore, the Council of the Galaxy Union has decided on a peaceful and impartial way for those species to continue living on safe planets.

00:09:19.710 --> 00:09:23.200
This is a matter that involves that planet alone.

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:25.160
It's none of our concern.

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:26.930
Fool.

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:32.460
Falam Orbius is a planet with the most wisdom and strongest military force within the Milky Way.

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:34.170
You would not stand a chance if they invaded.

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:41.180
It even took the Council of the Galaxy Union, through countless negotiations, much effort to make them agree to these terms.

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:45.700
A peaceful and impartial method.

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:52.930
The outcome will be decided, not with the clash of weapons, but with the clash of physical abilities of those planets' residents.

00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:56.860
By avoiding war, there is no longer a risk of harming the planet itself.

00:09:56.860 --> 00:10:01.060
It will decide the surviving species without resorting to wasteful mutual killing.

00:10:01.060 --> 00:10:05.000
This is the ideal answer that we have come upon.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:09.960
In other words, a soccer tournament involving the planets of the galaxy.

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:13.520
Grand Celesta Galaxy.

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:18.030
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:23.180
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:10:25.460 --> 00:10:29.310
In other words, a soccer tournament involving the planets of the galaxy.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.270
Grand Celesta Galaxy.

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.770
Unbelievable.

00:10:34.770 --> 00:10:39.780
You mean that this tournament decides who must surrender the right to live on their own planet.

00:10:40.150 --> 00:10:41.860
That it would be.

00:10:41.860 --> 00:10:46.010
The planet that ranks the highest in the tournament gets to choose which planet they can live on.

00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:47.750
That is the rule.

00:10:48.310 --> 00:10:52.750
Naturally, Falam Orbius is also participating to win.

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:54.750
It's all quite fair.

00:10:55.240 --> 00:11:00.970
Then if we don't rank the lowest, that would mean that we have protected our planet, correct?

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:02.220
Wrong.

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:02.760
What?

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:11.270
This galaxy may be vast, but very few of its planets meet the conditions that provide for intelligent life.

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:17.350
Accommodating all of Falam Orbius's inhabitants, who come from a giant planet,

00:11:17.350 --> 00:11:23.280
would require that they reside in nearly 99% of all relevant planets in this galaxy.

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:25.530
T-Then...

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:27.220
That's right.

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:32.290
Your only chance of keeping possession of this planet is by winning the championship.

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:41.480
Falam Orbius has already claimed their place in the finals by winning a separate block that has already taken place.

00:11:41.480 --> 00:11:48.010
Therefore, the only ones who can choose their planet before Falam Orbius does is the champion team.

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:51.890
If we don't win, Earth will be invaded by aliens?!

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:55.710
You ought to be grateful.

00:11:55.710 --> 00:12:02.200
All planets have been given a chance rather than be invaded one-sidedly.

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:17.290
Grand Celesta Galaxy...

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:21.800
A soccer tournament that extends throughout the galaxy, played by teams representing their planets...

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:25.340
If we don't participate, Earth will be destroyed...

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:27.850
If we lose, Earth will be invaded...

00:12:28.550 --> 00:12:33.310
This team was formed so that we win that tournament and save Earth.

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:36.330
The representatives for Earth, Earth Eleven.

00:12:36.330 --> 00:12:37.770
That is who you are.

00:12:38.930 --> 00:12:41.260
We're the Earth Eleven?

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:49.240
We're supposed to be in the preliminaries for the world tournament!

00:12:49.930 --> 00:12:58.380
No, what you were really in was the Galaxy Region A-Block's preliminaries for Grand Celesta Galaxy.

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:03.380
Which means our opponents up to now were all...

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:05.550
Yes.

00:13:05.550 --> 00:13:08.050
All of the teams were aliens.

00:13:16.130 --> 00:13:20.200
I knew there was something wrong. So that was it.

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:21.530
Aliens?

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:25.660
We were fighting things like that all this time?

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:26.530
Yeah...

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:31.510
But this is total nonsense.

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:36.520
No, it's a truth that none of us would have ever come upon through common sense.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:38.040
It's very interesting.

00:13:38.570 --> 00:13:43.640
Then I ask that all players make their preparations immediately.

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:47.430
You must prepare for your journey if you want to appear in the tournament.

00:13:48.080 --> 00:13:49.570
Journey?

00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:51.430
You mean, we're going to space?!

00:13:51.950 --> 00:13:52.820
What?!

00:13:52.820 --> 00:13:53.770
No way!

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:54.930
Impossible!

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:57.940
I can't...

00:14:27.730 --> 00:14:28.430
Huh?

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:35.930
Shun... Yuuta...

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:38.390
Tenma...

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:41.400
They all look so confused.

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:54.400
Coach, were you aware of this when you assembled us?

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:55.660
You hid the truth from us!

00:14:56.620 --> 00:15:01.170
If you knew the truth, would you have fought?

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:08.800
The decision to keep everything a secret so that you may fight was made by all of us.

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:09.380
That's right.

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:13.310
Who in their right minds would accept a reality such as this?

00:15:13.310 --> 00:15:18.950
Not only could I not find the right players, but I couldn't even find the right coach to lead the team.

00:15:18.950 --> 00:15:21.140
But then he appeared.

00:15:21.460 --> 00:15:23.480
Someone that I couldn't believe was alive.

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:26.350
So the rumors are true.

00:15:26.350 --> 00:15:28.450
Coach Kuroiwa Ryuusei.

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:30.110
You are really...

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:36.120
The emperor of darkness who menaced the soccer world in the past, Kageyama Reiji.

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:01.280
I understand the circumstances.

00:16:01.280 --> 00:16:03.190
I will take the position.

00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:05.020
You're...

00:16:05.620 --> 00:16:07.910
I was saved.

00:16:07.910 --> 00:16:11.680
My heart did stop momentarily.

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:15.730
But after that, measures were taken to resuscitate me back to life...

00:16:15.730 --> 00:16:18.120
Through forbidden means.

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:25.420
We're too late.

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:29.040
We've lost the patient.

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:30.600
A pity.

00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:31.640
Yes.

00:16:31.640 --> 00:16:34.930
Apparently he was the coach of the youth soccer team for Italy.

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:38.030
Edward.

00:16:38.460 --> 00:16:40.300
I have an idea.

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:42.890
Why don't we try using that?

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:44.640
That?

00:16:44.640 --> 00:16:45.600
You don't mean...?

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:53.130
I was used as an experiment for a new unapproved drug...

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:55.160
And strangely enough, came back from the dead.

00:16:56.570 --> 00:17:04.290
The trouble was that for the past 10 years, I've had to fake being a dead man.

00:17:10.400 --> 00:17:18.700
When we learned that Earth was on the verge of life or death, we needed someone who accepted this as fact and could lead a team.

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:24.370
The very man who arrived for this was 
Kageyama Reiji returned from the grave...

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:26.140
Now as Kuroiwa Ryuusei.

00:17:26.510 --> 00:17:29.350
Coach Kuroiwa, please tell us.

00:17:29.350 --> 00:17:30.860
Why did you choose these members?

00:17:31.710 --> 00:17:35.400
You needed a team that must fight while bearing the future of Earth on their shoulders.

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:37.360
Why these members?

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:39.150
He's right.

00:17:39.150 --> 00:17:43.110
It's true that each of them have great potential.

00:17:43.110 --> 00:17:46.870
But there were other players who are more suitable for this than these members.

00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:49.710
Coach!

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:51.750
Very well.

00:17:53.480 --> 00:18:01.320
Ever since that day when I looked death in the face, I've become able to see something I couldn't before.

00:18:01.570 --> 00:18:05.600
That is the beast that sleeps inside of people.

00:18:07.950 --> 00:18:09.060
Beast?

00:18:09.860 --> 00:18:16.740
Although it is faint, I am able to see the beast power that lurks within people.

00:18:17.970 --> 00:18:21.880
It is the very gene that this planet carries.

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:25.870
A power that only creatures of this planet possess.

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:37.510
Then, what happened with Konoha during the match, was that...?

00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:48.100
In ancient times, it was what we called a spiritual essence.

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:55.320
The power sleeping in Morimura's DNA has begun to awaken.

00:18:56.400 --> 00:19:05.490
By coming in contact with others who possess the genes of their planet, her self-defense instincts are awakening the beast power within her.

00:19:05.930 --> 00:19:08.450
There's a beast inside of me?

00:19:08.930 --> 00:19:16.550
All eleven of you here possess a great power that can help you fight species from other planets.

00:19:18.910 --> 00:19:22.510
We have that kind of power...

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:26.830
We leave the final decision to you.

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:30.130
Tenma.

00:19:30.130 --> 00:19:34.230
The weight of what we're responsible for in this fight is different from what we've had before.

00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:36.400
The future of Earth is at stake.

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:39.360
The future of Earth...

00:19:40.130 --> 00:19:43.120
We absolutely cannot afford to lose.

00:19:43.550 --> 00:19:45.610
What do you say, Tenma?

00:19:51.110 --> 00:19:53.670
If we can save Earth using soccer...

00:19:54.770 --> 00:19:58.000
If our soccer is what brings hope to Earth...

00:19:58.550 --> 00:20:00.880
Then we have to go out to space!

00:20:10.570 --> 00:20:16.680
Even if I say here that things will work out somehow, I don't think that will bring relief to any of us.

00:20:16.680 --> 00:20:20.860
But I want to find some way with all of you on how we can do something about this together!

00:20:25.220 --> 00:20:29.330
All I desire from you is that you keep winning.

00:20:29.710 --> 00:20:33.920
But do you honestly expect us to save Earth with just these members?

00:20:34.480 --> 00:20:35.460
No.

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:37.130
Not just these.

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:39.550
So you admit that we need additional members?

00:20:39.820 --> 00:20:41.330
T-That's...

00:20:43.910 --> 00:20:45.390
Hey, everyone.

00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:47.220
Endou-san!

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:50.930
Are <i>you</i>  the additional member?!

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:53.620
No, it's not me.

00:20:53.620 --> 00:20:56.940
It's this guy who will be joining you.

00:21:02.110 --> 00:21:05.740
My name is Ichikawa Zanakurou.

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:09.740
Ichikawa Zanakurou?

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:11.180
Yes.

00:21:12.400 --> 00:21:16.630
I will be playing soccer with all of you.

00:21:16.860 --> 00:21:19.420
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:21:19.640 --> 00:21:21.220
Huh?

00:21:21.220 --> 00:21:22.920
He looks oddly familiar...

00:22:54.310 --> 00:22:56.710
A surprising new member arrives!

00:22:56.710 --> 00:23:00.910
We go out on a journey, so long as there's a field there for us to fight on!

00:23:00.910 --> 00:23:03.240
Next, Let's Go! To Space!!

00:23:03.240 --> 00:23:05.530
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:19.580
The Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy's proverb today is...

00:23:23.310 --> 00:23:27.060
Our soccer is what brings hope to Earth!

00:23:27.060 --> 00:23:28.050
That's all!
